# 11. What I would make the actual research contribution

I would frame OASIS around this:

> **An energy-aware software optimization assistant that identifies runtime energy hotspots, diagnoses their underlying code-level causes, recommends evidence-backed transformations, and uses an LLM to implement developer-approved optimizations, with functional and empirical energy validation.**

The particularly interesting research problem is:

> **How can energy-aware optimization recommendations be made trustworthy without relying on repeated trial-and-error code generation and energy measurement?**

Your answer is:

```text
Real measurement
      +
Static/dynamic diagnosis
      +
Research-backed optimization evidence
      +
LLM implementation
      +
Final empirical validation
```

That is **much stronger conceptually** than "train XGBoost to predict energy."

